From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:16:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 015/201] Unified: context bar with the actions for what was
 picked, next to the cursor

When a face, edge, sketch or part is picked in the 3D view, a small bar
appears next to the cursor with what can be done with it right there:
a face can be sketched on, extruded, cut in or shelled, edges can be
filleted or chamfered, a sketch extruded, cut in, revolved or edited, a
part moved or hidden. The buttons run the ordinary commands, so their
task panels and drag handles work as usual. The bar hides when the
selection is cleared, a tool starts, or the view is orbited, panned or
zoomed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
